{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01MuqbCaZs1grEHMauvB8gcv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Typesafe & Fast as fuck Set in C\n2\t![](https://i.imgur.com/4JE58Ew.png)\n3\t\n4\t### Key Features\n5\t* Extremely fast non-cryptographic hash algorithm [XXHash](https://cyan4973.github.io/xxHash/)\n6\t* Complete Typesafe APIs\n7\t* **Double Hashing** to avoid both Primary & Secondary clustering\n8\t* **Robinhood Hash**(*in progress*) for near constant time access\n9\t* Iterators for streaming usecase\n10\t* Allows **Custom Hash** & **Custom Comparator**\n11\t* Single header file to rule them all 🚀 🚀 🚀\n12\t\n13\tGo to this [blogpost](https://robus.dev/typesafe-and-fast-as-fk-set-in-c) for more information and motivation for writing Set from scratch.\n14\t\n15\t### Getting Started\n16\t```c\n17\t#include <stdio.h>\n18\t#include \"cset.h\"\n19\t\n20\t// Declare Cset of int type\n21\tCset(int) cset_int_t;\n22\t// Declare Cset iterator of `cset_int_t` type\n23\tCset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n24\t\n25\tint main() {\n26\t    // Instance of cset_int_t\n27\t    cset_int_t cset_int;\n28\t\n29\t    // Initialize\n30\t    cset__init(&cset_int);\n31\t\n32\t    // Add elements\n33\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 1);\n34\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 2);\n35\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 2); // Duplicate\n36\t\n37\t    size_t size = cset__size(&cset_int);\n38\t    printf(\"Size of set is: %ld\\n\", size);\n39\t\n40\t    // Iteration\n41\t    cset_iterator_int_t cset_iterator_int;\n42\t\n43\t    // Initialize iterator with cset_int\n44\t    cset_iterator__init(&cset_iterator_int, &cset_int);\n45\t\n46\t    // Traverse\n47\t    for(;;) {\n48\t      if (cset_iterator__done(&cset_iterator_int)) break;\n49\t\n50\t      int* buffer;\n51\t      cset_iterator__next(&cset_iterator_int, buffer);\n52\t\n53\t      printf(\"Got: %d\\n\", *buffer);\n54\t    }\n55\t}\n56\t```\n57\t\n58\t###\n59\t### Installation\n60\tSimply copy paste `cset.h` in your source directly or you can use [Clib](https://github.com/clibs/clib) package manager for installation\n61\t```sh\n62\tclib install robusgauli/cset\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t### APIs\n66\t* `cset__add(cset, value)`: *no return*\n67\tAdd element to set.\n68\t    ```c\n69\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n70\t\n71\t    Cset(char) cset_char_t;\n72\t\n73\t    int main() {\n74\t      cset_char_t cset_char;\n75\t      cset__init(&cset_char);\n76\t\n77\t      // Add elements to set\n78\t      cset__add(&cset_char, 'a');\n79\t      cset__add(&cset_char, 'b');\n80\t    }\n81\t\n82\t    cset__free(&cset_int);\n83\t    ```\n84\t\n85\t* `cset__remove(cset, value)`: *no return*\n86\tRemoves element from the set.\n87\t\n88\t    ```c\n89\t    #include <assert.h>\n90\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n91\t\n92\t    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n93\t\n94\t    int main() {\n95\t      cset_int_t cset_int;\n96\t      cset__init(&cset_int);\n97\t\n98\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n99\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 1);\n100\t\n101\t      // Remove element from the set\n102\t      cset__remove(&cset_int, 34);\n103\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 0);\n104\t\n105\t      cset__free(&cset_int);\n106\t    }\n107\t    ```\n108\t* `cset__size(cset)`: *returns `size_t`*\n109\tReturns the size of set.\n110\t    ```c\n111\t    #include <assert.h>\n112\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n113\t\n114\t    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n115\t\n116\t    int main() {\n117\t      cset_int_t cset_int;\n118\t      cset__init(&cset_int);\n119\t\n120\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n121\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n122\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n123\t\n124\t      size_t size = cset__size(&cset_int);\n125\t      printf(\"Size: %ld\\n\", size);\n126\t\n127\t      cset__free(&cset_int);\n128\t    }\n129\t    ```\n130\t* `cset__clear(cset)`: *no return*\n131\tRemoves all the elements from the set.\n132\t    ```c\n133\t    #include <assert.h>\n134\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n135\t\n136\t    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n137\t\n138\t    int main() {\n139\t      cset_int_t cset_int;\n140\t      cset__init(&cset_int);\n141\t\n142\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n143\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n144\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n145\t\n146\t      // Clear the set\n147\t      cset__clear(&cset_int);\n148\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 0);\n149\t\n150\t      cset__free(&cset_int);\n151\t    }\n152\t    ```\n153\t\n154\t* `cset__contains(cset, value, flag)`: *no return*\n155\tTest whether an element is in set.\n156\t    ```c\n157\t    #include <assert.h>\n158\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n159\t\n160\t    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n161\t\n162\t    int main() {\n163\t      cset_int_t cset_int;\n164\t      cset__init(&cset_int);\n165\t\n166\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n167\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n168\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n169\t\n170\t      // Positive membership test\n171\t      bool contains = false;\n172\t      cset__contains(&cset_int, 34, &contains);\n173\t      assert(contains == true);\n174\t\n175\t      // Negative membershi test\n176\t      cset__contains(&cset_int, 100, &contains);\n177\t      assert(contains == false);\n178\t\n179\t      cset__free(&cset_int);\n180\t    }\n181\t    ```\n182\t* `cset__set_comparator` & `cset__set_hash()`: *no return*\n183\t\n184\t   **NOTE:** Both **Custom Comparator and Hash** must be implemented.\n185\t\n186\t    These above methods allows us to use custom hashing and comparator for complex structs. Please go through this [link](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2265503/why-do-i-need-to-override-the-equals-and-hashcode-methods-in-java) for why we need to implement both functions for correctness.\n187\t\n188\t    ```c\n189\t    #include <assert.h>\n190\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n191\t\n192\t    typedef struct {\n193\t      int x;\n194\t      int y;\n195\t    } Node;\n196\t\n197\t    // Custom comparator\n198\t    bool custom_comparator(Node* self, Node* other) {\n199\t      return (self -> x) == (other -> x);\n200\t    }\n201\t    // Custom hash function\n202\t    // It takes pointer to Node and function as an arguments\n203\t    cset__u64 custom_hash(Node* self, cset__u64 (*hash)(void*, size_t)) {\n204\t      // VVIP: Hash function requires pointer to data and the size in bytes\n205\t      return hash(&(self -> x), sizeof(self -> x));\n206\t    }\n207\t\n208\t    Cset(Node) cset_node_t;\n209\t\n210\t    int main() {\n211\t      cset_node_t cset_node;\n212\t      cset__init(&cset_node);\n213\t      cset__set_hash(&cset_node, custom_hash);\n214\t      cset__set_comparator(&cset_node, custom_comparator);\n215\t\n216\t      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=4,.y=5}));\n217\t      // Duplicate because our custom comparator and hash uses `x`\n218\t      // instead of whole struct for hash\n219\t      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=4,.y=4}));\n220\t\n221\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 1);\n222\t\n223\t      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=1, .y=2}));\n224\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 2);\n225\t\n226\t      // Removed because our comparator uses `x` i.e 1 which already exists\n227\t      cset__remove(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=1, .y=45}));\n228\t      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 1);\n229\t\n230\t      cset__free(&cset_node);\n231\t    }\n232\t    ```\n233\t\n234\t* `cset__free`: *no return*\n235\tFrees up heap allocation\n236\t\n237\t    ```c\n238\t    #include \"cset.h\"\n239\t\n240\t    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n241\t\n242\t    int main() {\n243\t      cset_int_t cset_int;\n244\t      cset__init(&cset_int);\n245\t\n246\t      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n247\t\n248\t      // Free up the memory\n249\t      cset__free(&cset_int);\n250\t    }\n251\t    ```\n252\t\n253\t### APIS for Iteration\n254\t\n255\t* `Cset_iterator(type)`\n256\t    Creates Iterator type definition for a given cset type.\n257\t\n258\t* `cset_iterator__init(iter, cset)`: *no return*\n259\t    Initializes iterator `iter` with `cset`.\n260\t  ```c\n261\t  #include \"cset.h\"\n262\t\n263\t  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n264\t  // 1. Define iterator type for `cset_int_t`\n265\t  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n266\t\n267\t  int main() {\n268\t    cset_int_t cset_int;\n269\t    cset__init(&cset_int);\n270\t\n271\t    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n272\t    // 2. Initialize iterator with `cset_int`\n273\t    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n274\t  }\n275\t  ```\n276\t\n277\t* `cset__done(iter)`: *returns `bool`*\n278\t    Returns whether the iteration is complete or not.\n279\t  ```c\n280\t  #include <assert.h>\n281\t  #include \"cset.h\"\n282\t\n283\t  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n284\t  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n285\t\n286\t  int main() {\n287\t    cset_int_t cset_int;\n288\t    cset__init(&cset_int);\n289\t\n290\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n291\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n292\t\n293\t    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n294\t    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n295\t\n296\t    // Checks whether the iteration is complete or not\n297\t    bool done = cset_iterator__done(&cset_int_iterator);\n298\t    assert(done == false);\n299\t  }\n300\t  ```\n301\t\n302\t* `cset__next(iter, buffer)`: *no return*\n303\t\n304\t    Yields pointer to next element into buffer. Note: buffer must be pointer type.\n305\t\n306\t  ```c\n307\t  #include <assert.h>\n308\t  #include \"cset.h\"\n309\t\n310\t\n311\t  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n312\t  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n313\t\n314\t  int main() {\n315\t    cset_int_t cset_int;\n316\t    cset__init(&cset_int);\n317\t\n318\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n319\t    cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n320\t\n321\t    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n322\t    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n323\t\n324\t    for (;;) {\n325\t      if (cset_iterator__done(&cset_int_iterator)) break;\n326\t\n327\t      // Yields pointer to next element into buffer\n328\t      int* buffer;\n329\t      cset_iterator__next(&cset_int_iterator, buffer);\n330\t\n331\t      printf(\"Got: %d\\n\", *buffer);\n332\t    }\n333\t\n334\t    cset__free(&cset_int);\n335\t  }\n336\t  ```\n337\t\n338\t### APIS for basic set operations\n339\t\n340\t* `cset__intersection(result, a, b)`: *no return*\n341\tPuts the intersection of two sets `a` and `b` in `result`.\n342\t\n343\t  ```c\n344\t  #include <assert.h>\n345\t  #include \"cset.h\"\n346\t\n347\t  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n348\t\n349\t  int main() {\n350\t    cset_int_t cset_int_a;\n351\t    cset_int_t cset_int_b;\n352\t\n353\t    cset__init(&cset_int_a);\n354\t    cset__init(&cset_int_b);\n355\t\n356\t    // Add elements to cset_int_a\n357\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 12);\n358\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 13);\n359\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 14);\n360\t\n361\t    // Add elements to cset_int_b\n362\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 12);\n363\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 13);\n364\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 16);\n365\t\n366\t    cset_int_t result;\n367\t    cset__init(&result);\n368\t\n369\t    // Perform intersection between cset_int_a and cset_int_b\n370\t    cset__intersect(&result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n371\t\n372\t    assert(cset__size(&result) == 2);\n373\t\n374\t    cset__free(&cset_int_a);\n375\t    cset__free(&cset_int_b);\n376\t    cset__free(&result);\n377\t  }\n378\t  ```\n379\t\n380\t* `cset__union(result, a, b)`: *no return*\n381\tPuts all the elements that are in either set into `result`\n382\t\n383\t  ```c\n384\t  #include <assert.h>\n385\t  #include \"cset.h\"\n386\t\n387\t  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n388\t  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n389\t\n390\t  int main() {\n391\t    cset_int_t cset_int_a;\n392\t    cset_int_t cset_int_b;\n393\t    cset_int_t cset_result;\n394\t\n395\t    cset__init(&cset_int_a);\n396\t    cset__init(&cset_int_b);\n397\t    cset__init(&cset_result);\n398\t\n399\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 34);\n400\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 25);\n401\t    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 12);\n402\t\n403\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 1);\n404\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 4);\n405\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 34);\n406\t\n407\t    // Perform union between `cset_int_a` and `cset_int_b`\n408\t    cset__union(&cset_result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n409\t\n410\t    // Size of the `cset_result` set must be 5 with elements { 34, 25, 12, 1, 4 }\n411\t    assert(cset__size(&cset_result) == 5);\n412\t\n413\t    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 100);\n414\t    cset__union(&cset_result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n415\t    // Size of the `cset_result` set must be 6 as we added new elements to `cset_int_b`\n416\t    assert(cset__size(&cset_result) == 6);\n417\t\n418\t    cset__free(&cset_int_a);\n419\t    cset__free(&cset_int_b);\n420\t    cset__free(&cset_result);\n421\t  }\n422\t  ```\n423\t\n424\t### License\n425\t\n426\tCopyright © 2020-20121 Robus, LLC. This source code is licensed under the MIT license found in\n427\tthe [LICENSE.txt]\n428\tThe documentation to the project is licensed under the [CC BY-SA 4.0](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\n429\tlicense.\n430\t\n431\t\n432\t---\n433\tMade with ♥ by Robus Gauli ([@robusgauli]\n434\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c87e10c8-a5fc-4c23-9bd1-a239e922f35f","uuid":"03db7e70-1210-4dd0-a906-239c704d143e","timestamp":"2026-05-29T09:34:47.208Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-iAd4uQ/project/c_src/README.md","content":"# Typesafe & Fast as fuck Set in C\n![](https://i.imgur.com/4JE58Ew.png)\n\n### Key Features\n* Extremely fast non-cryptographic hash algorithm [XXHash](https://cyan4973.github.io/xxHash/)\n* Complete Typesafe APIs\n* **Double Hashing** to avoid both Primary & Secondary clustering\n* **Robinhood Hash**(*in progress*) for near constant time access\n* Iterators for streaming usecase\n* Allows **Custom Hash** & **Custom Comparator**\n* Single header file to rule them all 🚀 🚀 🚀\n\nGo to this [blogpost](https://robus.dev/typesafe-and-fast-as-fk-set-in-c) for more information and motivation for writing Set from scratch.\n\n### Getting Started\n```c\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include \"cset.h\"\n\n// Declare Cset of int type\nCset(int) cset_int_t;\n// Declare Cset iterator of `cset_int_t` type\nCset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n\nint main() {\n    // Instance of cset_int_t\n    cset_int_t cset_int;\n\n    // Initialize\n    cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n    // Add elements\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 1);\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 2);\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 2); // Duplicate\n\n    size_t size = cset__size(&cset_int);\n    printf(\"Size of set is: %ld\\n\", size);\n\n    // Iteration\n    cset_iterator_int_t cset_iterator_int;\n\n    // Initialize iterator with cset_int\n    cset_iterator__init(&cset_iterator_int, &cset_int);\n\n    // Traverse\n    for(;;) {\n      if (cset_iterator__done(&cset_iterator_int)) break;\n\n      int* buffer;\n      cset_iterator__next(&cset_iterator_int, buffer);\n\n      printf(\"Got: %d\\n\", *buffer);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n###\n### Installation\nSimply copy paste `cset.h` in your source directly or you can use [Clib](https://github.com/clibs/clib) package manager for installation\n```sh\nclib install robusgauli/cset\n```\n\n### APIs\n* `cset__add(cset, value)`: *no return*\nAdd element to set.\n    ```c\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(char) cset_char_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_char_t cset_char;\n      cset__init(&cset_char);\n\n      // Add elements to set\n      cset__add(&cset_char, 'a');\n      cset__add(&cset_char, 'b');\n    }\n\n    cset__free(&cset_int);\n    ```\n\n* `cset__remove(cset, value)`: *no return*\nRemoves element from the set.\n\n    ```c\n    #include <assert.h>\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_int_t cset_int;\n      cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 1);\n\n      // Remove element from the set\n      cset__remove(&cset_int, 34);\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 0);\n\n      cset__free(&cset_int);\n    }\n    ```\n* `cset__size(cset)`: *returns `size_t`*\nReturns the size of set.\n    ```c\n    #include <assert.h>\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_int_t cset_int;\n      cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n\n      size_t size = cset__size(&cset_int);\n      printf(\"Size: %ld\\n\", size);\n\n      cset__free(&cset_int);\n    }\n    ```\n* `cset__clear(cset)`: *no return*\nRemoves all the elements from the set.\n    ```c\n    #include <assert.h>\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_int_t cset_int;\n      cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n\n      // Clear the set\n      cset__clear(&cset_int);\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_int) == 0);\n\n      cset__free(&cset_int);\n    }\n    ```\n\n* `cset__contains(cset, value, flag)`: *no return*\nTest whether an element is in set.\n    ```c\n    #include <assert.h>\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_int_t cset_int;\n      cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 25);\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n\n      // Positive membership test\n      bool contains = false;\n      cset__contains(&cset_int, 34, &contains);\n      assert(contains == true);\n\n      // Negative membershi test\n      cset__contains(&cset_int, 100, &contains);\n      assert(contains == false);\n\n      cset__free(&cset_int);\n    }\n    ```\n* `cset__set_comparator` & `cset__set_hash()`: *no return*\n\n   **NOTE:** Both **Custom Comparator and Hash** must be implemented.\n\n    These above methods allows us to use custom hashing and comparator for complex structs. Please go through this [link](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/2265503/why-do-i-need-to-override-the-equals-and-hashcode-methods-in-java) for why we need to implement both functions for correctness.\n\n    ```c\n    #include <assert.h>\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    typedef struct {\n      int x;\n      int y;\n    } Node;\n\n    // Custom comparator\n    bool custom_comparator(Node* self, Node* other) {\n      return (self -> x) == (other -> x);\n    }\n    // Custom hash function\n    // It takes pointer to Node and function as an arguments\n    cset__u64 custom_hash(Node* self, cset__u64 (*hash)(void*, size_t)) {\n      // VVIP: Hash function requires pointer to data and the size in bytes\n      return hash(&(self -> x), sizeof(self -> x));\n    }\n\n    Cset(Node) cset_node_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_node_t cset_node;\n      cset__init(&cset_node);\n      cset__set_hash(&cset_node, custom_hash);\n      cset__set_comparator(&cset_node, custom_comparator);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=4,.y=5}));\n      // Duplicate because our custom comparator and hash uses `x`\n      // instead of whole struct for hash\n      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=4,.y=4}));\n\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 1);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=1, .y=2}));\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 2);\n\n      // Removed because our comparator uses `x` i.e 1 which already exists\n      cset__remove(&cset_node, ((Node){.x=1, .y=45}));\n      assert(cset__size(&cset_node) == 1);\n\n      cset__free(&cset_node);\n    }\n    ```\n\n* `cset__free`: *no return*\nFrees up heap allocation\n\n    ```c\n    #include \"cset.h\"\n\n    Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n    int main() {\n      cset_int_t cset_int;\n      cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n      cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n\n      // Free up the memory\n      cset__free(&cset_int);\n    }\n    ```\n\n### APIS for Iteration\n\n* `Cset_iterator(type)`\n    Creates Iterator type definition for a given cset type.\n\n* `cset_iterator__init(iter, cset)`: *no return*\n    Initializes iterator `iter` with `cset`.\n  ```c\n  #include \"cset.h\"\n\n  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n  // 1. Define iterator type for `cset_int_t`\n  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n\n  int main() {\n    cset_int_t cset_int;\n    cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n    // 2. Initialize iterator with `cset_int`\n    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n  }\n  ```\n\n* `cset__done(iter)`: *returns `bool`*\n    Returns whether the iteration is complete or not.\n  ```c\n  #include <assert.h>\n  #include \"cset.h\"\n\n  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n\n  int main() {\n    cset_int_t cset_int;\n    cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n\n    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n\n    // Checks whether the iteration is complete or not\n    bool done = cset_iterator__done(&cset_int_iterator);\n    assert(done == false);\n  }\n  ```\n\n* `cset__next(iter, buffer)`: *no return*\n\n    Yields pointer to next element into buffer. Note: buffer must be pointer type.\n\n  ```c\n  #include <assert.h>\n  #include \"cset.h\"\n\n\n  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n\n  int main() {\n    cset_int_t cset_int;\n    cset__init(&cset_int);\n\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 34);\n    cset__add(&cset_int, 56);\n\n    cset_iterator_int_t cset_int_iterator;\n    cset_iterator__init(&cset_int_iterator, &cset_int);\n\n    for (;;) {\n      if (cset_iterator__done(&cset_int_iterator)) break;\n\n      // Yields pointer to next element into buffer\n      int* buffer;\n      cset_iterator__next(&cset_int_iterator, buffer);\n\n      printf(\"Got: %d\\n\", *buffer);\n    }\n\n    cset__free(&cset_int);\n  }\n  ```\n\n### APIS for basic set operations\n\n* `cset__intersection(result, a, b)`: *no return*\nPuts the intersection of two sets `a` and `b` in `result`.\n\n  ```c\n  #include <assert.h>\n  #include \"cset.h\"\n\n  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n\n  int main() {\n    cset_int_t cset_int_a;\n    cset_int_t cset_int_b;\n\n    cset__init(&cset_int_a);\n    cset__init(&cset_int_b);\n\n    // Add elements to cset_int_a\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 12);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 13);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 14);\n\n    // Add elements to cset_int_b\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 12);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 13);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 16);\n\n    cset_int_t result;\n    cset__init(&result);\n\n    // Perform intersection between cset_int_a and cset_int_b\n    cset__intersect(&result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n\n    assert(cset__size(&result) == 2);\n\n    cset__free(&cset_int_a);\n    cset__free(&cset_int_b);\n    cset__free(&result);\n  }\n  ```\n\n* `cset__union(result, a, b)`: *no return*\nPuts all the elements that are in either set into `result`\n\n  ```c\n  #include <assert.h>\n  #include \"cset.h\"\n\n  Cset(int) cset_int_t;\n  Cset_iterator(cset_int_t) cset_iterator_int_t;\n\n  int main() {\n    cset_int_t cset_int_a;\n    cset_int_t cset_int_b;\n    cset_int_t cset_result;\n\n    cset__init(&cset_int_a);\n    cset__init(&cset_int_b);\n    cset__init(&cset_result);\n\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 34);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 25);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_a, 12);\n\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 1);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 4);\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 34);\n\n    // Perform union between `cset_int_a` and `cset_int_b`\n    cset__union(&cset_result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n\n    // Size of the `cset_result` set must be 5 with elements { 34, 25, 12, 1, 4 }\n    assert(cset__size(&cset_result) == 5);\n\n    cset__add(&cset_int_b, 100);\n    cset__union(&cset_result, &cset_int_a, &cset_int_b);\n    // Size of the `cset_result` set must be 6 as we added new elements to `cset_int_b`\n    assert(cset__size(&cset_result) == 6);\n\n    cset__free(&cset_int_a);\n    cset__free(&cset_int_b);\n    cset__free(&cset_result);\n  }\n  ```\n\n### License\n\nCopyright © 2020-20121 Robus, LLC. This source code is licensed under the MIT license found in\nthe [LICENSE.txt]\nThe documentation to the project is licensed under the [CC BY-SA 4.0](http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\nlicense.\n\n\n---\nMade with ♥ by Robus Gauli ([@robusgauli]\n","numLines":434,"startLine":1,"totalLines":434}}}
